// # pulled/ — Per-Repo Documentation Sources
//
// Logline: The JSON files fetched by the SPA when a sub-menu item
//          is clicked. One file per route.
//
// Setup: Each file is a 3-section document (## What it is / ## Install
//        / ## Surface) with the same shape. The SPA fetches
//        `/pulled/{repo}.json`, renders the title + Source: line +
//        markdown content.
//
// Beats:
//   1. openOODA.json — the polyrepo front door (8 repos, install).
//   2. ooda.json     — the compiler/runtime substrate.
//   3. std.json      — the 8-domain standard library.
//   4. opm.json      — the content-addressed package manager.
//   5. cli.json      — the `ooda` binary driver.
//   6. lsp.json      — the language server.
//   7. mcp.json      — the MCP server for AI agents.
//
// oodac and runtime have no JSON yet — the SPA renders a "coming
// soon" placeholder for those two routes until the repos are
// extracted from ooda/.
//
// No build step today. Each file is hand-synced from the matching
// `openOODA/{repo}/docs/` source. A future `site_pull_repo_docs.oo`
// (not in this repo) would automate the sync.
